From 821dce1d503bf908960110288b655bd13789db2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:57:55 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 35/49] Switch Vulkan: dynamic resolution of the 3D view

Console logs (c391ba597): steady scenes run at 45-58 fps with the GPU at
10-14 ms, but Brutal Doom explosions (dozens of large translucent smoke
sprites) push the 3D scene past 16 ms and some frames to ~90 ms. The GPU
benchmark showed a 0.75 scale cuts 36% of the GPU time.

The main view is now drawn into a smaller part of the render target when
the GPU frame time (timestamps) exceeds rd_dynres_target (12 ms): the
scale follows the scene's share of the frame, drops at most 20% per step,
and climbs back 5% after 30 calm frames (rd_dynres_min 0.6). It is
stretched back with a linear blit right after the scene, before the
weapon sprites and the HUD, which stay at full resolution. No buffers are
recreated. perf.log reports the average and minimum 3D resolution;
rd_dynres_force fixes the scale for tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
